\section*{Projects}
\smallskip
\entry{Anti Collision System using Monocular Depth Estimation}{Apr 2025 -- May 2026 \\ \textbf{Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu, India} \textbf{\textbar{}} \href{https://1drv.ms/f/c/b8d0d879c4c6b5cb/IgDdZxFmi9bIRLfppk8r4VRhAWm9g_mbB61_vDr_gSDBixU?e=m9Tljg}{Link}}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Python, Anaconda IDE, Nvidia Jetson Orin Nano, Monocular Camera, ADAS, LLM (Large Language Models), Deep Learning, Artificial Intelligence}
  \item This project developed a low cost, camera only anti collision system for Advanced Driver Assistance Systems (ADAS). It implemented and benchmarked two monocular depth estimation models as alternatives to costly LiDAR and stereo camera setups: Monodepth2, a self supervised CNN encoder decoder, and DPT-Hybrid, a transformer based architecture using attention. Both were trained and evaluated on the KITTI autonomous driving dataset with standard preprocessing (resizing, pixel normalization, augmentation) and further validated on a custom collected ``Campus Dataset''. The pipeline paired YOLOv8/YOLOv10 object detection with the depth models to produce real time, per object distance estimates, and was deployed end to end on an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano for embedded, hardware in the loop inference. Key challenges included the inherent ambiguity of recovering 3D depth from a single 2D image, training without labeled depth data via self supervised photometric loss, balancing accuracy against computational cost for real time deployment (Monodepth2 at ${\sim}$14.5--26M parameters vs.\ DPT-Hybrid at ${\sim}$123M), and maintaining robustness under night time glare and low visibility. Performance was measured against LiDAR ground truth using standard depth estimation metrics: Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), Absolute Relative Error (AbsRel), and $\delta_1$ (accuracy). Across 154 test frames, DPT-Hybrid significantly outperformed Monodepth2 (RMSE 1.91 vs.\ 5.73; AbsRel 0.144 vs.\ 0.596; $\delta_1$ 0.837 vs.\ 0.450), though Monodepth2's smaller footprint proved more practical for embedded deployment. Real world testing achieved average distance detection accuracy of 86\% or higher with a static camera and 75\% or more when both object and camera were moving, with reliable detection ranges of 3--24\,m in daytime and 3--9\,m at night. This demonstrates that monocular depth estimation can serve as a viable, cost effective solution for real time collision avoidance in ADAS. To contextualize the cost advantage, the monocular approach cut hardware cost by roughly 96\%, about 1/27th the cost of the LiDAR sensor alone, or roughly 26--27$\times$ cheaper.
\end{itemize}

\entry{\\Stock Market Prediction Using Deep Learning}{May 2025 -- Jul 2025 \\ \textbf{Indian Statistical Institute, Kolkata, India} \textbf{\textbar{}} \href{https://1drv.ms/f/c/b8d0d879c4c6b5cb/IgAltXJOMi_BRp3m9-xDmrGzASn_fKkUzRaPmS4RXXiqqRw?e=Q4AVrY}{Link}}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Python, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Accurate LSTM Forecasting}
  \item This project develops a sophisticated deep learning model for accurate stock market prediction. Leveraging Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) networks, the model excels at capturing complex temporal dependencies and historical patterns within financial data. A key innovation is its focus on identifying universal market patterns across diverse datasets, enabling robust predictions for any new, unseen company. Our methodology involves rigorous data preprocessing like handling missing values and data normalization using MinMaxScaler class from scikit learn, comprehensive model training, and performance evaluation using metrics like Mean Squared Error and Mean Absolute Error. The LSTM model demonstrated superior accuracy and efficiency compared to alternative approaches such as CNN model based stock market prediction wherein the MSE improved from 0.0028 to 0.00036 (or 87\%) and MAE improved from 0.0299 to 0.0103 (or 66\%). It is designed to forecast 30 day stock prices. An intuitive HTML/CSS/JavaScript front end provides seamless user interaction for company selection and prediction visualization. The Flask API framework powers the back end, handling core logic, prediction services, and data management or alternatively Streamlit can also be used. This system provides an adaptable, and accessible tool for advanced financial analytics, offering immediate insights into market trends. Looking ahead, the framework is designed to evolve toward universal market generalization, enabling reliable forecasts for new, unseen companies beyond the currently trained sectors adapting to unique market dynamics through advanced cross market analysis.
\end{itemize}

