\entry{\\Signal BOOSTER X: Expanding the Reach of Weak Signals}{Dec 2023 -- Mar 2024 \\ \textbf{Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham} \textbf{\textbar{}} \href{https://1drv.ms/f/c/b8d0d879c4c6b5cb/IgD1WGNPHW6zSbjuiS8w77dTAajvoABR8zxhYoCiVDjsmGk?e=V1xXNx}{Link}}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Python, Signal Processing}
  \item Amidst the rapid evolution of wireless technology, signal dead zones remain a major challenge, especially indoors and in weak coverage areas. Signal Booster X is a low cost dual antenna cellular/Wi-Fi signal amplification system designed to capture, amplify, and rebroadcast weak signals. The input antenna captures the signal and directs it to the amplification stage, while the output antenna retransmits the amplified signal. The MediaTek MT7528 KN chipset manages wireless communication, data processing, and connectivity, while a Python based monitoring application provides real time signal strength and network speed measurements. The system uses a signal enhancement and interference suppression algorithm to coordinate signal acquisition, filtering, amplification, and stabilization. It applies gain where required while suppressing unwanted interference and unnecessary noise amplification, with basic spectrum management and error correction mechanisms for stable connectivity. Python based speed testing further showed that downlink speed increased from 15.541 Mbps to 17.817 Mbps, an improvement of 2.276 Mbps, while uplink speed increased from 1.266 Mbps to 30.095 Mbps, an improvement of 28.829 Mbps.
\end{itemize}

\entry{\\Ficomtoo: Lossless Text File Compression}{Dec 2023 -- Mar 2024 \\ \textbf{Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham} \textbf{\textbar{}} \href{https://1drv.ms/f/c/b8d0d879c4c6b5cb/IgBmFxpcXPaTTId07us6JP2QAYW8-R7mIPh3ST37exEcrCg?e=aqxEXD}{Link}}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Python, Huffman Coding Technique, Data Structures and Algorithms}
  \item Ficomtoo is a Python based lossless text file compression and decompression system utilizing Huffman coding to achieve optimal data compression. The project implements core data processing features such as frequency analysis, binary Huffman tree construction, variable length code generation, and custom mapping tables to replace symbols with shorter binary codes. Performance testing successfully demonstrated the system's efficiency by reducing an input text file size from 1.76 KB (1,803 bytes) down to 1.27 KB (1,301 bytes) which is approximately 27 percent decrease.
\end{itemize}

