\section*{Publications}

\entry{CampusDepth-A-Large-Scale-Day-Night-RGB-Dataset-for-Monocular-Depth-Estimation}{May 2026}
\entrymeta{Mendeley Data \textbar{} \href{https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/dg5zcsd952/1}{Link}}
\begin{itemize}
  \item Advanced Driver Assistance Systems (ADAS) require accurate and reliable perception of the surrounding environment to ensure vehicle safety and reduce the risk of collisions. Depth estimation plays a crucial role in understanding object distance and spatial relationships in traffic scenes. This dataset focuses on the preliminary data analysis required for the development of a low cost, camera based anti collision system using monocular depth estimation to address the limitations of conventional depth sensing methods.
  \item The dataset includes 21 daytime recorded videos of daytime scenarios and 10 recorded videos of night time scenarios taken across different locations inside Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu. The videos have dataset markings spread across 3 m starting from 0 m to 30.
  \item The videos are then sampled across various time instants leading to a total of 1,08,634 image frames combined across daytime and night time scenarios. The camera was setup and placed on a tripod to ensure smooth and stable video readings. The videos were recorded as .mp4 format and images as .jpeg format
  \item The study emphasizes the importance of conducting a comprehensive statistical and performance analysis on large scale datasets collected across a finite spatial domain within the campus environment.
\end{itemize}

